---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { title, editions, editors, sources, publisher, bookCitation } from '../../data/catalogue.mjs';
const edition = editions['2e'];
const schema = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Book', name: title, bookEdition: '2', isbn: edition.isbn, copyrightYear: edition.year, editor: editors.map(e => ({ '@type': 'Person', name: e.name, url: e.url })), publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: publisher } };
---
<Layout title="The handbook" active="The book" schema={schema}>
  <div class="wrap book-hero"><figure class="book-display"><img src={edition.cover} alt="The second-edition book cover" width="640" height="960" /></figure><div class="book-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Second edition · 2024</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="editor-credit">Edited by Natalie M. Scala<br />and James P. Howard, II</p><p>The handbook brings together authored chapters on analytical approaches, applications, and professional practice. The second edition places the contributions in three parts: Approaches, Applications, and Soft Skills and Perspectives.</p><dl class="book-metadata"><div><dt>Publisher</dt><dd>{publisher}</dd></div><div><dt>Print ISBN</dt><dd>{edition.isbn}</dd></div><div><dt>Contents</dt><dd>20 chapters · 3 parts</dd></div></dl><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href={sources.second}>Visit the publisher <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/chapters/">Explore the contents</a></div></div></div>
  <div class="wrap book-information"><section class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">A reference for the work</p><h2>Methods, settings, and experience.</h2><p>An edited handbook gives readers more than one entrance to a field. A particular method may be the right starting point for one reader; another may recognize a planning problem or a difficulty in getting a model used. The companion preserves the book’s chapter structure while making those other entrances visible. Contributor pages identify who wrote each chapter, and the reading room offers a small set of clearly labeled editorial routes through the chapter topics.</p><p>The publisher’s page is the place to check available formats, access arrangements, and ordering information. This website does not sell the book or host its full text. Publication details on this page follow the publisher’s second-edition listing; the separate first-edition archive preserves the earlier contents.</p><p class="source-note">Publication source: <a href={sources.second}>Chapman &amp; Hall/CRC, second edition</a>.</p></section><section class="citation-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Reference the volume</p><h2>Cite the handbook.</h2><p id="book-citation">{bookCitation('2e')}</p><div class="citation-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-copy="book-citation">Copy citation</button><span role="status" class="small" aria-live="polite"></span></div><p class="citation-downloads"><a href="/citations/second-edition.bib" download>BibTeX</a><a href="/citations/second-edition.ris" download>RIS</a></p><p class="small">For a particular contribution, cite its chapter authors as well as the edited volume. Confirm the chapter’s page range in your copy.</p></section></div>
  <section class="wrap archive-feature"><img src={editions['1e'].cover} alt="First-edition cover" width="120" height="180" loading="lazy" /><div><p class="eyebrow">The earlier collection · 2020</p><h2>The first edition has its own history.</h2><p>Its four-part organization, chapter titles, and bylines are kept separate from the current edition.</p><a class="text-link" href="/book/first-edition/">Explore the first-edition archive <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
</Layout>
